// Position coach's pre-draft interview script.


Coach Reyes looks up from his draft board as you approach.
"Ah. Our next prospect. Let's see what you've got on tape."

* [Coach, what are you looking for out here?]
    "Looking for? Football IQ. Most guys around here just run fast."
    Do you know how to read a defense before the snap?
    * * [Yes! I study film every night.]
        "Good. That's the difference between a fifth round guy and a franchise player."
        -> END
    * * [Not really, but I'm a fast learner.]
        "Fair enough. Ball don't care about resume. Show me how you play on the field."
        -> END

* [Just here to run my drills, Coach.]
    "Fine by me. Numbers talk at the combine."
    Watch your footwork on the three-cone drill. That's where most prospects fall apart.
    -> END
